<!-- ll-card demo — mirrors the upstream docs page (#/components/card).
     All docs-page examples are in: Settings (Preview), Stat cards, Guest
     book, Article card, On every stock, Pinned/clipped/stapled, Login,
     Create project. -->
<view class="demo">
  <ll-page-title underline="highlight" seed="card" custom-style="margin-bottom:16rpx;">Card</ll-page-title>
  <view class="sec-desc">A card is a sheet of paper: header, title, description, action, content and footer with shadcn's spacing, on any stock and edge. Dividers are drawn pencil rules, and a card can be taped, pinned or clipped to the desk.</view>

  <view class="sec sec--grid">
    <view class="sec-h2">Preview</view>
    <view class="sub-h3">Settings card</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">The whole family: a title and description, an action tucked into the header, content, and a footer with a pencil rule above it.</view>
    <view class="stack-card">
      <ll-card seed="settings">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-title>Notifications</ll-card-title>
          <ll-card-description>Choose what lands in your inbox.</ll-card-description>
          <ll-button slot="action" variant="link" size="sm">Reset</ll-button>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <view class="set-row" wx:for="{{settings}}" wx:key="id">
            <text class="set-label">{{item.label}}</text>
            <ll-switch checked="{{item.on}}" data-id="{{item.id}}" bind:change="onSettingChange" aria-label="{{item.label}}" />
          </view>
        </ll-card-content>
        <ll-card-footer rule="pencil" custom-style="justify-content:flex-end;gap:16rpx">
          <ll-button variant="ghost" size="sm">Cancel</ll-button>
          <ll-button size="sm">Save</ll-button>
        </ll-card-footer>
      </ll-card>
    </view>
  </view>

  <view class="sec sec--grid">
    <view class="sec-h2">Examples</view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Stat cards</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">Index cards for one number each. The figures are set in the script font with tabular numerals; the trend says up or down in words, not only in color.</view>
    <view class="stack-card">
      <ll-card stock="index-card" seed="Pages written" custom-style="gap:24rpx;padding:40rpx 0">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-description>Pages written</ll-card-description>
          <ll-card-title custom-style="font-size:54rpx;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums lining-nums">1,284</ll-card-title>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <text class="stat-trend" style="color:#3b7a4b">up 12% on last week</text>
        </ll-card-content>
      </ll-card>
      <ll-card stock="index-card" seed="Drafts open" custom-style="gap:24rpx;padding:40rpx 0">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-description>Drafts open</ll-card-description>
          <ll-card-title custom-style="font-size:54rpx;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums lining-nums">17</ll-card-title>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <text class="stat-trend" style="color:#c2412d">down 3 since Monday</text>
        </ll-card-content>
      </ll-card>
      <ll-card stock="slip" seed="Words per day" custom-style="gap:24rpx;padding:40rpx 0">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-description>Words per day</ll-card-description>
          <ll-card-title custom-style="font-size:54rpx;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums lining-nums">640</ll-card-title>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <text class="stat-trend" style="color:#4a433c">steady</text>
        </ll-card-content>
      </ll-card>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Guest book</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A form on a guest check: green ledger paper, a perforated top, a dashed footer. The fields are ordinary labeled inputs; the sheet only changes the paper they are written on.</view>
    <view class="stack-sm">
      <ll-card stock="check" seed="guest">
        <ll-card-header rule="dashed">
          <ll-card-title>Sign the guest book</ll-card-title>
          <ll-card-description>Name, and one line for the wall.</ll-card-description>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content custom-style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32rpx">
          <view class="field">
            <text class="label">Name</text>
            <ll-input placeholder="Ada" value="{{guestName}}" bind:input="onGuestName" aria-label="Name" />
          </view>
          <view class="field">
            <text class="label">A line for the wall</text>
            <ll-input placeholder="Lovely evening." value="{{guestLine}}" bind:input="onGuestLine" aria-label="A line for the wall" />
          </view>
        </ll-card-content>
        <ll-card-footer rule="dashed" custom-style="justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16rpx">
          <text class="gb-no">No. 0042</text>
          <ll-button size="sm" bind:tap="onSign">Sign</ll-button>
        </ll-card-footer>
      </ll-card>
      <text class="status" aria-live="polite">{{guestStatus}}</text>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Article card</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A card taped at the corners with a torn bottom edge, for something you would pin above your desk.</view>
    <view class="stack-md">
      <ll-card tape="both" tape-kind="washi-dots" edge="{{articleEdge}}" seed="article" custom-style="padding-bottom:64rpx">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-description>Notebook - 4 min read</ll-card-description>
          <ll-card-title custom-style="font-size:52rpx">Why the margin is the best part</ll-card-title>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <text class="article-p">Most of what I remember from a book is in the margins: an arrow, a question mark, a small argument with a dead author.</text>
        </ll-card-content>
        <ll-card-footer custom-style="justify-content:flex-start">
          <ll-button variant="link" size="sm" custom-style="margin-left:-24rpx">Keep reading</ll-button>
        </ll-card-footer>
      </ll-card>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">On every stock</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A card is a sheet of paper, so it takes any stock, edge and printed rules: graph paper, a dot grid, kraft, an index card with a torn top.</view>
    <view class="stocks-grid">
      <ll-card wx:for="{{stocks}}" wx:key="title" stock="{{item.stock}}" rules="{{item.rules}}" edge="{{item.edge}}" seed="{{item.title}}" custom-style="gap:16rpx;padding:40rpx 0">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-title>{{item.title}}</ll-card-title>
          <ll-card-description>{{item.stock}}</ll-card-description>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <text class="stock-note">pencil, ink and a little tea</text>
        </ll-card-content>
      </ll-card>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Pinned, clipped, stapled</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">The `fastener` slot holds a card down. Calm density hides every prop, so a dense dashboard keeps its plain sheets.</view>
    <view class="fastener-grid">
      <ll-card wx:for="{{fasteners}}" wx:key="*this" fastener="{{item}}" seed="{{item}}" custom-style="gap:16rpx;padding:96rpx 0 48rpx">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-title>{{item}}</ll-card-title>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <text class="stock-note">held with a {{item === 'binder-clip' ? 'binder clip' : item}}</text>
        </ll-card-content>
      </ll-card>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Login</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">The shadcn demo: a title, a description, a link tucked into CardAction, a form of two labeled fields with a "forgot" link beside the second label, and a footer of two full-width buttons. Nothing is drawn but the paper, the fields and the buttons.</view>
    <view class="stack-card">
      <ll-card seed="login">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-title>Login to your account</ll-card-title>
          <ll-card-description>Enter your email below to login to your account</ll-card-description>
          <ll-button slot="action" variant="link" size="sm">Sign up</ll-button>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content custom-style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:48rpx">
          <view class="field">
            <text class="label">Email</text>
            <ll-input placeholder="m@example.com" value="{{loginEmail}}" bind:input="onLoginEmail" aria-label="Email" />
          </view>
          <view class="field">
            <view class="field-row">
              <text class="label">Password</text>
              <text class="link">Forgot your password?</text>
            </view>
            <ll-input password placeholder="" value="{{loginPw}}" bind:input="onLoginPw" aria-label="Password" />
          </view>
        </ll-card-content>
        <ll-card-footer custom-style="flex-direction:column;gap:24rpx;align-items:stretch">
          <ll-button custom-style="width:100%">Login</ll-button>
          <ll-button variant="outline" custom-style="width:100%">Login with Google</ll-button>
        </ll-card-footer>
      </ll-card>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Create project</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">The shadcn demo: a card around a small form. A text field, a Select (its list opens in `position="popper"` so it lines up with the trigger) and a footer with the two answers pushed apart. Deploy reports what it would do.</view>
    <view class="stack-card">
      <ll-card seed="create">
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-title>Create project</ll-card-title>
          <ll-card-description>Deploy your new project in one click.</ll-card-description>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content custom-style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32rpx">
          <view class="field">
            <text class="label">Name</text>
            <ll-input placeholder="Name of your project" value="{{cpName}}" bind:input="onCpName" aria-label="Name" />
          </view>
          <view class="field">
            <text class="label">Framework</text>
            <ll-select id="card-select" options="{{frameworks}}" value="{{cpFramework}}" placeholder="Select" aria-label="Framework" custom-style="width:100%" bind:change="onFramework" />
          </view>
          <text class="status" aria-live="polite">{{cpStatus}}</text>
        </ll-card-content>
        <ll-card-footer custom-style="justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16rpx">
          <ll-button variant="outline" size="sm" bind:tap="onCancel">Cancel</ll-button>
          <ll-button size="sm" bind:tap="onDeploy">Deploy</ll-button>
        </ll-card-footer>
      </ll-card>
    </view>
  </view>
</view>
